librknnrt (2.3.2-1+rkr7.20250408.e50bab8) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Built from mixtile-sdk-rk-rknpu2 e50bab83ae3c1a2c93be478a8292f0b04d8ddfc3,
    the linux-6.1-stan-rkr7 branch of Mixtile's mirror of the Rockchip SDK.
  * The tree carries no debian/, so all of it is ours. There is also nothing
    to compile: librknnrt.so is a prebuilt closed-source blob and this
    package puts it, its headers and rknn_server where they belong.
  * One package rather than the two radxa-pkg/rknn2 ships. Its
    rknpu2-rk3588 and rknpu2-rk356x exist because that SDK had two
    incompatible variants of the library -- its own lintian override says
    so. This SDK has a single runtime/Linux/librknn_api/aarch64/librknnrt.so
    for both SoCs; only the models differ, and models are not in here.
  * The blob's SONAME is librknnrt.so, with no version in it, so the two
    cannot be co-installed and the bare .so symlink has to live in the
    runtime package rather than in -dev. radxa's librknnrt.so.1 symlink is
    left out: nothing records that soname, so nothing looks for it.

 -- Mixtile <dev@mixtile.com>  Tue, 08 Sep 2026 08:00:00 +0000
